id: pm-csv-0orl
title: csv validate fails to register on pm-cli 2026.7.27 because it redeclares the host-owned --json global
description: "pm-cli 2026.7.27 (GH-719) makes the host reject any extension command whose flags shadow a host-owned global. csv validate declared { long: \"--json\" }, so registerCommand threw and the command failed to register against a real host. The suite never caught it because every smoke test asserted against a hand-rolled api double that accepts all registrations unconditionally. Fix: drop the flag declaration, read ctx.global.json, and rebuild the smoke suite on the SDK createExtensionTestHarness so pm's real activation engine validates registration."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-07-27T04:48:48.376Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-27T04:48:55.108Z"
author: codex
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-27T04:48:55.107Z",codex,"Verified end-to-end in a throwaway workspace: pm install reports failed_count: 0; 'pm csv validate data.csv' and '--json' both work reading the host global; 'pm csv import' round-trips 2 real rows. Suite 105/105."
body: ""
